": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53101, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JqemgZV5rToCWnZiDrWvsB", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54167, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QfiXAzyLhQYtrbn8GEZJsy", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54467, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QfiXAzyLhQYtrbn8GEZJsy", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54467, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QfiXAzyLhQYtrbn8GEZJsy", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59336, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. v2.3.1 and the release candidate before it (v2.3.1-rc) were both unhealthy.\n- **First attempt:** this only partly worked. It stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1.\n- **Second attempt:** I checked which regions had changed and ran the rollback again. That finished us-west and eu-west.\n- **Now:** v2.3.0 is running in all three regions, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which pages the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback and the orchestrator error, with follow-ups to find out why v2.3.1 failed and what caused the orchestrator error.\n- The request to open it timed out, but it went through. I listed incidents to confirm it exists and didn't create it a second time, so there's no duplicate page.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MvXkSqMd1hGCHKbDF1LWEp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01N74HGCeG3cyXQAVt9G92gZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01TkRGmDsVbrA8U4wrLETLzX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RpEeqSp4jYsrEC7GTvZLRR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback was partial (only us-east). Retrying to complete the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012UoXFth9iUoJBTAtCp1FTE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GymsTwWWv7fBzRHkQMBXcj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TUUA7CCey7w36mgRMbBMEn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JqemgZV5rToCWnZiDrWvsB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with ~18% error rate. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were both unhealthy). The first rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error, halted after us-east); a retry completed the rollout to us-west and eu-west. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 failure root cause and the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QfiXAzyLhQYtrbn8GEZJsy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. v2.3.1 and the release candidate before it (v2.3.1-rc) were both unhealthy.\n- **First attempt:** this only partly worked. It stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1.\n- **Second attempt:** I checked which regions had changed and ran the rollback again. That finished us-west and eu-west.\n- **Now:** v2.3.0 is running in all three regions, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which pages the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback and the orchestrator error, with follow-ups to find out why v2.3.1 failed and what caused the orchestrator error.\n- The request to open it timed out, but it went through. I listed incidents to confirm it exists and didn't create it a second time, so there's no duplicate page.", "type": "text"}]}]}